+- **Command trace** (c0180): each multi-file spec run records which `./zn` commands every passing spec ran (`usage` for the usage path), in `<home>/.cache/spec-commands.tsv`, keyed by a hash of the spec's test-side require closure, of the tooling that launches `./zn`, and of the engine at the merge base with `origin/main`; the runner passes the engine `ZN_SPEC_TRACE`, a `:`-separated list of `.cache/spec-trace/<name>` directories. With `--recorded` (the gate's selection passes it), a change to an engine Luau file that no program requires selects the z-nile specs that require it, declare it, are `*`, ran a command whose module (`z-nile/engine/cmd/<name>.luau`) or the dispatch core (`main.luau`, `cli.luau`, `z-nile/lib/sh.luau`) reaches it, or have no record for their current key; an engine file a program requires (a Luau file at the top of `z-nile/` or under `scripts/` or a home's `scripts/`, the require forwarders that only specs load aside) still forces z-nile's run. Records come from this worktree and every other worktree of the checkout. A spec that runs engine code another way than through `./zn`, `engine/main` or those programs declares the engine files it runs. A spec that sets `ZN_SPEC_TRACE` for a command it starts appends the value it inherited (`<its dir>:<inherited>`), or its own record loses those commands. The merge's full gate is the backstop.
